  :adr/decision-summary
  "{:mapping {:mail-inbound [:mail-drain :-> \"refs/itonami/proposals/inbox/<msg-id>\" :proposal-commit],
              :agent-proposal [\"refs/itonami/proposals/<lane>/<id>\" :rationale :risk-tier],
              :governor :pre-merge-required-check,
              :approve [:signed-ff-only-merge :-> \"refs/itonami/<lane>/main\"],
              :execute [:post-merge :itonami-runner :handler :dedupe-by-effect-id],
              :audit [\"refs/itonami/audit/main\" :append-only]}
    :backend {:git [:kotoba-git :kotoba-rad], :replica :kotobase-private-tenant,
              :local-ledger :kotoba-ledger-file-git, :heavy [:datalad :git-annex :b2],
              :github :public-code-mirror-only, :p2p-replication :blocked-until-rad-r2,
              :secrets :alias-only}
    :permissions {:identity :did-key, :chain [:org-root :dept-delegate :employee],
                  :resource \"itonami://<org>/<repo>/<lane>\",
                  :abilities [:propose :review :merge :execute :read],
                  :dept [:lane-set :isco-blueprint],
                  :risk-tiers {:read-only :auto-merge-after-governor,
                               :external-send :one-lane-merge-signer,
                               :financial :two-signers-lane+keiei-no-self-approve,
                               :destructive :org-root-only},
                  :separation-of-duties {:proposer :propose-only, :approver :merge-only, :runner-bot :execute-only},
                  :revocation [:expiry-max-90d :journal-remove-delegate]}
    :runner {:trigger [:signed-head-announce :poll], :verify [:sigref :cacao-chain :risk-signatures],
             :fail-closed true, :receipt :audit-commit, :projection :git->store}
    :stages {:m0 :approval-dual-write-to-file-git,
             :m1 [:ops-repo :signed-refs :composed-push-gate-authorize-ref-update?],
             :m2 [:itonami-runner :mail-drain-emits-proposals],
             :m3 [:kotobase-authoritative :git-write-model :rad-r2-encrypted-replication]}
    :rejected {:github-actions :private-data+workflow-scope+sovereignty,
               :store-only :no-signed-attribution,
               :radicle-proper :kotoba-rad-exists,
               :drop-store :keep-as-read-model,
               :acl-only :capability-must-bind-to-merge-signature}
    :new-implementation [:composed-push-gate :itonami-runner :merge-signing-ui]
    :follow-ups [:m0-wiring-pr :authorize-ref-update?-upstream :org-root-key-ops :dept-lane-capability-edn :merge-ui-adr :rad-r2-tracking]}"
  :adr/addendum-2026-07-15-ops-drain-nbb-port
  {:summary "Closed the follow-up the 2026-07-14 nbb-send addendum itself
             flagged as the last remaining JVM-only entry point: 唯一残る
             JVM-only は inbound mail の Datom store 投影 (-M:ops-drain).
             scripts/mail-drain.cljs previously shelled out to `clojure
             -M:ops-drain` as a subprocess for exactly this reason; it now
             calls cloud-itonami.ops-drain/drain! directly in-process,
             matching how ops-cli.cljs already calls the outbound send
             path natively -- inbound now has no JVM in its path either."
   :real-gaps-found-and-closed
   ["cloud-itonami.store's open-file-conn/save-file-conn! had NO :cljs
     branch at all (JVM-only java.io), unlike the near-identical
     cloud-itonami.ops-store which already had one for the ops-repo db.
     Added the same EDN-via-Node's-fs pattern; a .bin path now throws a
     clear error under cljs (JVM ObjectOutputStream format has no cljs
     counterpart) instead of being silently unreachable"
    "cloud-itonami.mail had an unconditional (require [cheshire.core :as
     json] ...) plus several functions already documented in a comment as
     JVM-only (ingest-file!/jvm-http-fn/send-message-via-resend!/
     send-via-resend!/send-marketing-outreach!/mail/-main) but never
     actually reader-conditional-wrapped -- so the WHOLE namespace failed
     to even compile under cljs, blocking ops-drain's own require of it.
     Wrapped the documented JVM-only section in one #?(:clj (do ...))
     block; record->inbound/inbound->tx (the only fns ops-drain calls)
     were already portable"
    "cloud-itonami.ops-keys turned out to already be FULLY portable
     (ops-cli.cljs's outbound path already calls it under cljs) --
     ops_drain.cljc's own #?(:clj [cloud-itonami.ops-keys :as ops-keys])
     require wrapping was unnecessarily conservative, not a real blocker.
     Removed it, and fixed a related small inconsistency: drain-records!
     passed :runner-seed #?(:clj (ops-keys/runner-seed) :cljs nil), so an
     inbound-drain receipt would go UNSIGNED under cljs while outbound
     (which calls the same fn unconditionally) always signs -- now calls
     it unconditionally too, matching outbound"]
   :verification
   {:full-suite "clojure -M:test: 834 tests / 6886 assertions, 6 failures
                 (same 6 pre-existing, unrelated failures as a clean-clone
